.Dd $Mdocdate: November 24 2026 $
.Dt LIBANSILOVE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libansilove
.Nd Library for converting ANSI, ASCII, and other formats to PNG
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In ansilove.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a library to convert ANSi and artscene related file formats into PNG
images, supporting ANSI (.ANS), PCBoard (.PCB), Binary (.BIN), Artworx
(.ADF), iCE Draw (.IDF), Tundra (.TND) and XBin (.XB) formats.
.Pp
It produces size-optimized indexed-color PNG images for most formats,
with truecolor output when requested or required.
It also supports 80x25 and 80x50 PC fonts (including all 14 MS-DOS
character sets), Amiga fonts, and iCE colors.
.Pp
All library functions take a context, defined as an
.Em ansilove_ctx
structure in
.In ansilove.h :
.Bd -literal
struct ansilove_ctx {
        uint8_t *buffer;
        size_t maplen;
        size_t length;
        struct ansilove_png png;
        uint8_t error;
};
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Va ctx->png
member stores the encoded PNG image and its length in bytes:
.Bd -literal
struct ansilove_png {
        uint8_t *buffer;
        int length;
};
.Ed
.Pp
Options are passed to the different loaders using the
.Em ansilove_options
structure in
.In ansilove.h :
.Bd -literal
struct ansilove_options {
        bool diz;
        bool dos;
        bool icecolors;
        bool truecolor;
        int16_t columns;
        uint8_t font;
        uint8_t bits;
        uint8_t mode;
        uint8_t scale_factor;
};
.Ed
.Ss Context lifecycle
Allocate a context and options structure, then call
.Xr ansilove_init 3 .
Set rendering options, load an input file with
.Xr ansilove_loadfile 3 ,
and call the renderer for its format.
The library does not automatically select a renderer from a filename.
After successful rendering, save the PNG with
.Xr ansilove_savefile 3
or consume
.Va ctx->png.buffer
and
.Va ctx->png.length
directly.
.Pp
Once
.Xr ansilove_init 3
has succeeded, release resources with
.Xr ansilove_clean 3
after each conversion, including if loading or rendering fails.
Loading or rendering again does not release the previous mapping or PNG
buffer.
Clean and reinitialize the context before starting another conversion.
Pointers into either buffer must not be used after cleanup.
.Ss Rendering options
The
.Xr ansilove_init 3
function initializes the options structure to zero, except for
.Va bits ,
which is set to 8.
Renderers may update option fields, including filling in a default column
count and enabling truecolor when ANSI input requests RGB colors.
.Bl -tag -width scale_factor
.It Va diz
Crop ANSI output to the used columns, up to the configured column count.
.It Va dos
Apply DOS aspect ratio correction by vertically resampling the image
by a factor of 1.35.
.It Va icecolors
Enable high-intensity background colors in ANSI and Binary input.
.It Va truecolor
Use a truecolor canvas for ANSI rendering.
RGB color sequences also enable this option automatically.
.It Va columns
Number of character columns for ANSI, Binary, PCBoard, and TundraDraw.
Zero selects 80 columns, except for Binary, which defaults to 160.
Explicit values must be between 1 and 4096.
Other formats derive their dimensions from the input.
.It Va font
Select a built-in font using an
.Dv ANSILOVE_FONT_*
constant from
.In ansilove.h .
Used by ANSI, Binary, PCBoard, and TundraDraw.
Zero selects the standard IBM PC 80x25 font.
.It Va bits
Character cell width, in pixels, for ANSI, Binary, PCBoard, and TundraDraw.
Must be 8 or 9.
.It Va mode
Zero selects normal rendering.
.Dv ANSILOVE_MODE_CED
and
.Dv ANSILOVE_MODE_WORKBENCH
select alternative rendering modes for ANSI input.
CED mode uses black text on a gray background and a width of 78 columns,
unless
.Va diz
is enabled.
Workbench mode uses the Amiga Workbench palette.
.Dv ANSILOVE_MODE_TRANSPARENT
marks color zero as transparent during output processing.
.It Va scale_factor
Integer image scaling factor, applied after DOS aspect ratio correction.
Zero disables scaling; supported factors are 2 through 8.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ansilove_ansi 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_artworx 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_binary 3 ,
